SUMMARY:Wild Neighbors Library Tour (Swannanoa)
DESCRIPTION:Join Swannanoa Valley WILD! in partnership with Friends of the WNC Nature Center as we get WILD at the Swannanoa Public Library. Participants will have the opportunity to meet reptile and amphibian animal ambassadors as we explore the important connection between wildlife and habitat. After our animal ambassador program\, we’ll venture to the garden to discuss pollinators\, native plants\, and maybe even get our hands a little dirty! This is a great opportunity for families with kids ages K – 6th grade.  \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/wild-neighbors-library-tour-swannanoa/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/wnclibrary.jpg
END:VEVENT
