CREATED:20260428T150549Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T150550Z
UID:10001597-1778612400-1778617800@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Invasive Plant Species: Mecklenburg & Beyond (Charlotte)
DESCRIPTION:You’re invited to a hands-on presentation with NCWF Charlotte Wildlife Stewards Chapter. Discover invasive plant species firsthand and learn about their life history. Chapter leader Ed Murray will lead the way as we explore the intersection of humans\, habitat\, and invasive plants. \nAs our population grows\, so too does our need for space and development. Balancing growth and development with the needs of wildlife is paramount. How do we create spaces in our yards\, neighborhoods\, parks\, and cities that work with wildlife\, not against wildlife? What are the invasive species that stand in our way\, and how do we identify and remove them? \nYou won’t want to miss out as we explore all these topics and more during this engaging presentation. Folks in attendance will receive automatic entry into a raffle and door prize! See you there. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/invasive-plant-species-mecklenburg-beyond-charlotte/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/InvasivePlantSpeciesEdMurray.png
END:VEVENT
